// Type-checks the tests, which the emitting project cannot.
//
// `../tsconfig.json` must stay `include: ["src/**/*"]` with `rootDir: "src"`:
// that is what makes `out/extension.js` land where package.json's `main`
// points, and adding `test/**` to it would emit test JS into `out/`, which
// `.vscodeignore` does not exclude — so test JavaScript would ship inside the
// .vsix. Hence a second, non-emitting project rather than a wider include.
// It lives in `test/` rather than as a root `tsconfig.test.json` because
// `.vscodeignore` excludes `test/**` but names `tsconfig.json` literally, so a
// root sibling would itself ship (verified with `vsce ls`).
//
// Both overrides below are load-bearing, and dropping either yields a check
// that cannot report a real error:
//   - `exclude` must be re-stated, because `extends` inherits
//     ["node_modules", "out", "test"] and `exclude` filters `include` —
//     inheriting it drops every test file straight back out of the program,
//     leaving a step that exits 0 with four blatant type errors in the tree.
//   - `rootDir` must be overridden, not omitted, because `extends` inherits
//     "src" and every test file then reports TS6059 instead of its real
//     diagnostics.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".."
  },
  "include": ["../src/**/*", "**/*"],
  "exclude": ["../node_modules", "../out"]
}
